🎵 CWPP MUSIC PROMPT — Melancholic Acoustic Ballad (Mid-60s British)

Core Emotional Constraint (HIGH WEIGHT)
Quiet regret and reflective melancholy, intimate and inward-facing. The performance feels like a private confession recorded late at night, emotionally restrained rather than dramatic.

Tempo & Meter (LOCKED)
Slow to mid-slow tempo (~95–100 BPM)
4/4 time
Gentle forward pulse, no rhythmic urgency
Harmony & Tonality (HIGH WEIGHT)
Centered in a warm major key with frequent modal borrowing into minor
Chord progressions emphasize descending bass motion and unexpected minor turns
Harmonies feel “sad despite being major,” with cadences that resolve softly rather than triumphantly
Instrumentation (CRITICAL CONSTRAINT)
Solo acoustic guitar (steel-string), fingerpicked
Sparse string quartet (violins + viola + cello) used as emotional shading, not melody drivers

NO drums
NO bass guitar
NO keyboards

Arrangement Rules
Guitar establishes the harmonic bed from the first second
Strings enter subtly after the opening phrase, swelling only at emotional peaks
Strings should feel cinematic but restrained — short legato phrases, no ostinatos
Silence and space between phrases are intentional and expressive

Vocal Delivery (VERY HIGH WEIGHT)
Single male vocal, close-mic’d
Soft, slightly weary tone
Minimal vibrato, natural phrasing
Emotion comes from phrasing and breath, not power
Performance feels reflective, almost apologetic

Melodic Shape
Narrow melodic range
Stepwise motion dominates
Occasional upward leap used sparingly for emotional emphasis, then gently falls back down
Production & Era Texture
Mid-1960s analog studio warmth
Mono or narrow stereo field
Light tape saturation
No modern polish, no heavy reverb — intimacy over size
Structural Constraint

Short song form (~25 SECONDS)
No instrumental solos
Each section feels like a continuation of the same emotional thought rather than contrast
Lyrical Placeholder Guidance (DO NOT COPY ORIGINAL LYRICS)
Themes: lost love, hindsight, things that felt easier “before”
Language is simple, conversational, almost diary-like
No metaphors that are too abstract or poetic — clarity over cleverness

Overall Intent (SUMMARY LOCK)
A timeless acoustic lament where sadness hides inside a major key, supported by delicate strings, delivered with humility and restraint — a song that feels older than the listener, as if it has always existed.